{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/741758-athanor-preview","id":741758,"title":"Athanor Preview","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-30T07:59:10-07:00","id":741758,"title":"Athanor Preview","content":"Declaring victory, going home, wait, already there. <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/prometheaninto-the-furnace/#comment-453601\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/prometheanint...comment-453601</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":969,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","user":"Verge","date":". 10-30-2015, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T08:35:28-07:00","id":741871,"title":"","content":"Hmm... what is this Azothic memory the preview speaks of? Now I'm really curious about the other stuff going on with Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T08:55:43-07:00","id":741967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/741758-athanor-preview?p=741871#post741871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... what is this Azothic memory the preview speaks of? Now I'm really curious about the other stuff going on with Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Azothic memory's been discussed a little, but it's been a while. Basically, Prometheans carry with them some instinctive understanding of the Pilgrimage and how to approach it; the universal milestones, the five basic Refinements, and so on. They can delve into Azothic memory a bit more if they want, and there's a whole section of Transmutations designed around doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T09:00:30-07:00","id":741976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/741758-athanor-preview?p=741967#post741967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Azothic memory's been discussed a little, but it's been a while. Basically, Prometheans carry with them some instinctive understanding of the Pilgrimage and how to approach it; the universal milestones, the five basic Refinements, and so on. They can delve into Azothic memory a bit more if they want, and there's a whole section of Transmutations designed around doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're like (magically reanimated, divine fire-leaking, stitched-together) salmon. I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T09:08:03-07:00","id":741984,"title":"","content":"I really like the idea of taking someone else's torments (little t) in order to understand yourself. It is a beautiful analogy for walking a mile in someone's shoes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T09:21:52-07:00","id":742005,"title":"","content":"The bit about the Vitriol Fount intrigues me. Is Vitriol still going to be a special kind of experience that collects Beats, or is each individual Beat going to be like a point of something like Pyros? Because in 1e you could spend Vitriol like it was Pyros if you needed to and it becomes Reagent when left in an Athanor- so what is it now, I wonder?<br /> <br /> Ooh, I just had a thought. Azoth remembers all these things, it's a kind of collective unconscious of the Divine Fire that retains the memories of everything that has ever used Pyros. Every Promethean, every Alchemist, every <i>qashmal</i>. The Principle is on a Pilgrimage too. What are we teaching It? What will It become?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T11:08:40-07:00","id":742272,"title":"","content":"So as Athanors we get something like mages Soul Stones and no Z-Splat for Created? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I can favor this items &quot;to help in Pilgrimage&quot; ( even if the <i>really</i> looks like 1:1 copy from Soul Stones), but what about &quot;special groups&quot; for Prometheans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-30-2015, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T11:17:04-07:00","id":742310,"title":"","content":"Well...they weren't Special Groups in the first edition either, they were more of a Soul Mould. The only known group for Prometheans are the Pilgrims, following the Seer. There are such a small number of Prometheans at any given time that forcing groups on them would feel out of place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T11:23:28-07:00","id":742327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/741758-athanor-preview?p=742272#post742272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So as Athanors we get something like mages Soul Stones and no Z-Splat for Created? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I can favor this items &quot;to help in Pilgrimage&quot; ( even if the <i>really</i> looks like 1:1 copy from Soul Stones), but what about &quot;special groups&quot; for Prometheans?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't see the point of adding a z-splat to represent &quot;special groups&quot; when we already have refinements and advanced refinements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T11:28:22-07:00","id":742337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/741758-athanor-preview?p=742327#post742327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't see the point of adding a z-splat to represent &quot;special groups&quot; when we already have refinements and advanced refinements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought they are on same &quot;level&quot; - like Y-Splats - only that Basic Refinements are those starting. From what I know about 2ED, <i>any</i> Created can choose <i>any</i> Refinement, be it Basic or Advanced. They just cannot start from Advanced. So Advanced Refinements are not really <i>&quot;special&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> Not to mention we do not have place for &quot;special rules groups&quot;, like niche sects or characters with unique mechanics. When I cannot make something in normal <b>Vampire</b> or <b>Mage</b> setting - like unique antagonists powers - I just work on the Bloodline or Legacy. Without Z-Splat in <b>Promethean</b>, we cannot make things like this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-30-2015, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T11:37:50-07:00","id":742354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/741758-athanor-preview?p=742337#post742337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought they are on same &quot;level&quot; - like Y-Splats - only that Basic Refinements are those starting. From what I know about 2ED, <i>any</i> Created can choose <i>any</i> Refinement, be it Basic or Advanced. They just cannot start from Advanced. So Advanced Refinements are not really <i>&quot;special&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> Not to mention we do not have place for &quot;special rules groups&quot;, like niche sects or characters with unique mechanics. When I cannot make something in normal <b>Vampire</b> or <b>Mage</b> setting - like unique antagonists powers - I just work on the Bloodline or Legacy. Without Z-Splat in <b>Promethean</b>, we cannot make things like this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if you need an enemy with weird powers you can just make a regular character and give them weird powers.<br /> <br /> In the God-Machine Chronicle, one of the villains was some sort of perfectly resurrected <i>thing</i> that the G-M empowered to go kill stuff. It had some Numina, but wasn't an angel, that it powered with Willpower.<br /> <br /> Promethean just doesn't seem like a game that would have or even need a z-splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T15:27:41-07:00","id":743035,"title":"","content":"If we <i>had</i> to have a z-splat, I think the way to go would be something like a Kindred bloodline: A subset of your Promethean Lineage that offers unusual powers for Prometheans of your type (say there was a subset of Galateids that was more fearful than appealing, or Osirans that could reincarnate into new bodies instead of returning to their original). Like Bloodlines, you could have it within your Divine Fire from your creator, learning by sharing in the Azoth of a member (Avus-equivalent), or found your own by refining your Pyros through study, practice and meditation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T16:38:17-07:00","id":743214,"title":"","content":"Athanors were sort of an afterthought to begin with; justified more by the pattern set by the previous games than by anything they added by themselves. The old school Athanors look like they still exist in Refinement Furnaces, but now alongside other expressions.<br /> <br /> BlackHatMatt in the comments: &quot;If Prometheans reach their Z-splat, they win.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T17:09:33-07:00","id":743265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/741758-athanor-preview?p=742337#post742337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought they are on same &quot;level&quot; - like Y-Splats - only that Basic Refinements are those starting. From what I know about 2ED, <i>any</i> Created can choose <i>any</i> Refinement, be it Basic or Advanced. They just cannot start from Advanced. So Advanced Refinements are not really <i>&quot;special&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> Not to mention we do not have place for &quot;special rules groups&quot;, like niche sects or characters with unique mechanics. When I cannot make something in normal <b>Vampire</b> or <b>Mage</b> setting - like unique antagonists powers - I just work on the Bloodline or Legacy. Without Z-Splat in <b>Promethean</b>, we cannot make things like this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Geist</b>, <b>Mummy</b>, <b>Demon</b>, and <b>Beast</b> all lack 'special rules groups.' While I hope z-splats aren't a design feature of the past never to be seen again and while I'd like to see them in one or two of the aforementioned games, they admittedly aren't necessary in every game. I'd argue they aren't even necessary in some of the games that <i>do</i> feature them.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness is a weird place with all kinds of creatures representing exceptions to the Rules and weird sub-set cliques. There's no reason you couldn't throw in a 'special rules' group yourself (as I've done with <b>Mummy</b>), though I do know it's nice to have it published for us. At any rate, this whole kind of idea is what <b>Night Horrors</b> books are about, and a <b>Promethean Night Horrors</b> book is something Matt has coincidentally been pitching for a long while<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T17:41:04-07:00","id":743311,"title":"","content":"Athanors to me have always felt as an extra tool for the Promethean's tool box and a very minor consolidation prize upon &quot;winning&quot;<br /> <br /> Extra resources, Not able to be possessed by things, etc. Interesting but given how rare the process is, It makes more sense to have these things actually more involved with the Pilgrimage than as a bit of a tacked on consolidation. Still doesn't break the game if some benefit after being human remains (very minor ones) but still nice overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T22:11:37-07:00","id":743859,"title":"","content":"I like many of the Redeemed Boons that 1e devised for its Athanors; but I'm quite content to see them divorced from Athanors in 2e. Instead, I like the notion of retasking them as possible rewards that can be earned in a particularly successful New Dawn. Say, instead of an exceptional success on the Final Azoth roll giving you immunity to Disquiet, Quiescence, Lunacy, and presumably Sybaris, give the player the option to acquire the equivalent of one Redeemed Boon of his choice. That said, I'd lean toward Redeemed Boons that grant benefits that can be found among the existing mortal population (e.g., any Merit that isn't Supernatural; a shift in your Attributes; a cash windfall). I'd tend to discourage ones that are essentially supernatural powers. <br /> <br /> And while I'm on the subject of what rewards you should receive with the New Dawn, I'd like to see a massive revision to what the Final Azoth Roll gives you: rather than the primary benefit being a restoration of your memory of your Promethean days, I'd like to see it recast in terms of being given an identity within mortal society. Fail the final Azoth roll, and you're an amnesiac vagrant who has no family or friends and no idea where he came from; succeed the roll, and you remember that your wife and kids are waiting for you at home, or your coworker finds you and reminds you that you don't want to be late for work. Oh, and I wouldn't allow any do-overs on said roll: that virtually guarantees success for anyone who Redeemed with more than a dot or two of Azoth. <br /> <br /> Regaining your memories of your previous existence as a Promethean might not even be a function of the Final Azoth Roll at all; it might be the result of stumbling across an Athanor, or more generally being exposed to a manifestation of Pyros (such as a Firestorm, a <i>qashmal</i>, or one of your former throng). Consider tying it to a botched Disquiet check, even.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T23:58:09-07:00","id":743915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/741758-athanor-preview?p=743311#post743311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extra resources, Not able to be possessed by things, etc. Interesting but given how rare the process is, It makes more sense to have these things actually more involved with the Pilgrimage than as a bit of a tacked on consolidation. Still doesn't break the game if some benefit after being human remains (very minor ones) but still nice overall.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I really miss - 2ED Athanors do not connect you with your post-New Dawn, leaving only marks for <i>others</i> Created to go in your footsteps. They should be yours alchemical furnaces, not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T11:42:35-07:00","id":744764,"title":"","content":"All I want from the New Dawn is a fresh start. Having the Pyros carve you a niche is too much for my liking, as I think it's better and more thematic to simply stumble out of it a freshly made mortal whose vulnerability awakens empathy and kindness in a way unknown to a former Promethean. Consider that a Promethean fights to join Humanity so that she may have a say in where she lives, and who she befriends. A prefab life should scare the hell out of any newly Redeemed.<br /> <br /> However, I do like the idea of a Redeemed being able to access memories, as well as Pyros and Transmutations, by getting ahold of a new-style Athanor. &quot;We're getting the band back together,&quot; and so forth. With a huge cost to Integrity, of course. They start to pick at the solidity of their real, established mortal existence, with its muddy morality and fading shine, and start longing for the urgency and clarity of the Pilgrimage. The remembrance of power, of the strength to bend bars and control men's minds, starts to invade their moral existence, and it seems all so easy just to go into work Monday and Mesmerize your ass a raise, or a promotion, or a date with the hot District Manager. To Break Bad, as it were, with some midlife crisis using stolen Vitriol, and risk the one prize that was ever worth anything to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T15:30:14-07:00","id":745255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/741758-athanor-preview?p=744764#post744764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I want from the New Dawn is a fresh start. Having the Pyros carve you a niche is too much for my liking, as I think it's better and more thematic to simply stumble out of it a freshly made mortal whose vulnerability awakens empathy and kindness in a way unknown to a former Promethean. Consider that a Promethean fights to join Humanity so that she may have a say in where she lives, and who she befriends. A prefab life should scare the hell out of any newly Redeemed.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify: I wasn't suggesting that the Promethean wouldn't have any say in who she befriends or where she lives, or that she'd be handed a prefab life. Rather, I was thinking in terms of taking social ties that the Promethean had pursued during her Pilgrimage and making them real. That, and giving the Promethean a birth certificate, driver's license, and/or other documentation that gives her a shot at living a normal life. I'm homeless right now, and I can tell you that not having a permanent residence when filling out paperwork is a major hurdle to getting ahead \u2014 not to mention the problem of not having a reliable place to bed down for the night. <br /> <br /> Which brings me to the bit about &quot;vulnerability awakens empathy and kindness&quot;. In my experience, this rarely happens. What happens is that self-righteous citizens who pigeonhole you into a \u201cworthless vagrant\u201d stereotype call the cops to get you out of their neighborhood. And bear in mind that I'm better off than most: I have an SUV and a job (two, actually) that provides me with food and shelter; there are others who don't even have <i>that</i> much. This should <i>not</i> be where the typical Redeemed finds himself right after the New Dawn: his &quot;fresh start&quot; should include enough standing in society that his mortal existence isn't \u201cthe Pilgrimage, part two\u201d \u2014 because even <i>without</i> Torment and Disquiet messing things up further, this lifestyle isn't a start of anything; it's a pit that can suck you in and chew you up if you're not careful. <br /> <br /> And that's the <i>real</i> world, before adding the trademark cynicism of the World of Darkness. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/741758-athanor-preview?p=744764#post744764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I do like the idea of a Redeemed being able to access memories, as well as Pyros and Transmutations, by getting ahold of a new-style Athanor. \u201cWe're getting the band back together,\u201d and so forth. With a huge cost to Integrity, of course. They start to pick at the solidity of their real, established mortal existence, with its muddy morality and fading shine, and start longing for the urgency and clarity of the Pilgrimage. The remembrance of power, of the strength to bend bars and control men's minds, starts to invade their moral existence, and it seems all so easy just to go into work Monday and Mesmerize your ass a raise, or a promotion, or a date with the hot District Manager. To Break Bad, as it were, with some midlife crisis using stolen Vitriol, and risk the one prize that was ever worth anything to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I do think, just for the sake of keeping the troupe together through the endgame, there should be an option that lets a Redeemed get involved in her former throng again, letting her serve as a helping hand in getting the others across the finish line. Which is not to say that there wouldn't be consequences for doing so: <i>in general</i>, letting the Promethean world back into your life is going to take a toll on you, even <i>if</i> you have a way of avoiding such obvious pitfalls as Disquiet slowly turning you against the Prometheans you're trying to help. <br /> <br /> More generally, I think <b>Promethean</b> would do well to have a section of advice on what comes after the New Dawn \u2014 <i>primarily</i> from the perspective of how the troupe moves forward in an endgame scenario where one of the protagonists may have just been retired. That is, what does the player do now that his character is out of the game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T17:14:50-07:00","id":745355,"title":"","content":"Well, the preview on 2e Athanors was something I've been looking forward to for <i>months</i>. And I got to admit, it didn't fail to impress with its concepts. Still looking for more clarification on the mechanics behind Refinement Furnaces, but I think the 1e Athanors could be house-ruled to exist in the same setting as the 2e ones?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/741758-athanor-preview?p=743915#post743915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This I really miss - 2ED Athanors do not connect you with your post-New Dawn, leaving only marks for <i>others</i> Created to go in your footsteps. They should be yours alchemical furnaces, not?</div> </div> </div> </div>For my take on it, I'd probably change the Azoth requirements from being what's needed to determine what kind of Athanor you can build, to being <i>how many</i> Athanors of their variety a Promethean can incorporate into their being. This is somewhat based on what I know of the Seba used by the Deceived in Mummy: The Curse. The difference here is that these Athanors don't produce any ill effects for the Created (unless someone brainstorms one).<br /> <br /> That said, under this homebrew system, a Promethean can possess a number of these internal Athanors (reflected as two and/or three dot Merits) equal to their dots in Azoth. The increasing strength in his Divine Fire does become a hindrance, at a certain point, but it can be used to create minor alchemic reactions in his body that have similar utility as the standard Transmutations. Additionally, I might also suggest that conversions of the 1e Athanors be bumped up slightly in terms of their power. And, maybe, like the 2e Changeling kiths seen so far, their effects can be rather innovative in their nature.<br /> <br /> A category of Athanor based on 1e should also include an updated system for reagents. I'm torn between giving a fixed pool of five points per dot of the character's Azoth, and sticking to the system of banking Vitriol to slowly build up your pool. The first option could fit if the EXP used to create the Athanor/s is <i>always</i> Vitriol. And the fixed five points per Athanor could also be further justified if they're bumped up to being a five-dot Merit in terms of cost. I'd appreciate additional thoughts on this.<br /> <br /> Lastly, Athanors converted from 1e may or may no longer be tied exclusively to a Lineage. Granted, some might be chosen more often by a single Lineage than others, but there should be no reason that a Wretched can't develop the benefits of the Unicorn (Muse) or Eagle (Nepri). And then there's a need for a name of this proposed type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T18:53:16-07:00","id":745524,"title":"","content":"Being objects now makes me wonder if alchemists can interact with them. Any benefits to their evil arts. I can definitely see these antagonists staking out known pilgrimage sites for 'raw materials' to show up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T23:07:50-07:00","id":745924,"title":"","content":"Well, I'll miss the mythological beast symbolism of 1e Athanors, but that should be an easy enough thing to retain on an ad hoc basis. These Athanors are way more useful as storytelling tools, so I will live.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T07:47:03-08:00","id":746592,"title":"","content":"I like how Prometheans in 2e are looking to have these little uplifting possibilities and points of guidance in their difficult journey that they lacked in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T09:40:12-08:00","id":746834,"title":"","content":"A lot of these little things were integrated in a sloppy way in my campaigns, because they seem necessary in order to have a fun game. This is shaping up to be a wonderful game. Can't wait!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T11:37:24-08:00","id":747115,"title":"","content":"I think we can keep or reintroduce the 1e Athanors just fine by the Refinement Furnace. It shows it's possible to build a Athanor benefiting only yourself.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T02:19:53-08:00","id":748778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/741758-athanor-preview?p=747115#post747115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we can keep or reintroduce the 1e Athanors just fine by the Refinement Furnace. It shows it's possible to build a Athanor benefiting only yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather <i>other</i> Athanor kind - the possible 1ED reintroduction would need to lock some experiences of Pilgrimage in it in the way of Merit, not of the Refinement itself. Pitty, we will need house rule for it as &quot;weird shamanistic animalism&quot; maybe is not good idea to game about alchemy - <i>but</i> the idea that you are preparing yourself for the next life you spend one life pursuing with usage of Athanors is rather suitable, ( Even if I like other usage of 2ED Athanors mentioned in preview. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-03-2015, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T21:58:21-08:00","id":750702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/741758-athanor-preview?p=748778#post748778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rather <i>other</i> Athanor kind - the possible 1ED reintroduction would need to lock some experiences of Pilgrimage in it in the way of Merit, not of the Internment itself. Pitty, we will need house rule for it as &quot;weird shamanistic animalism&quot; maybe is not good idea to game about alchemy - <i>but</i> the idea that you are preparing yourself for the next life you spend one life pursuing with usage of Athanors is rather suitable, ( Even if I like other usage of 2ED Athanors mentioned in preview. )</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The animal symbolism could be reserved for local use in certain parts of the globe, perhaps. And as for using animals in Alchemy...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.levity.com/alchemy/animal.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.levity.com/alchemy/animal.html\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Not Found </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.levity.com/alchemy/animal.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.levity.com/alchemy/animal.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T23:30:19-08:00","id":750778,"title":"","content":"Yep. The bestiary-style naming convention of 1e's Athanors wasn't a digression from the alchemy-themed elements in the rest of the book; it was a continuation of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T21:26:14-08:00","id":752997,"title":"","content":"Odd, I thought I had posted a response in this thread. Anyway, mythical animal themes in alchemy are often referential, rather than essential, as in animism. The Fox or the Rabbit are tied to tales that make up the culture that tell them, in &quot;shamanistic&quot; societies. In alchemy, the same animal might encompass the folk tales, but the importance lies in the material and processes that are symbolized. The Fox is a solar creature, referring to gold and fire, and are thought to have the secret of the Elixir of Life. To an alchemist, that's not about chasing fox-spirits and meditating on the morals of the fable. To him, the Fox represents an alchemical mystery, or a process, or a ritual. To the Promethean, this could mean a Refinement Furnace of Aurum, or possibly Phosphorum or Mercurius, which reveals the secret of the Fox symbol. Fox sometimes slips the sick and elderly doses of the Elixir, so maybe he learns Medicine, or gains curative powers. There <i>could</i> be communions with Fox the spirit, but what it should have to teach the Promethean will have little to do with the Pilgrimage (Fox's lessons are rarely beneficial).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T23:23:02-08:00","id":753104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/741758-athanor-preview?p=752997#post752997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Odd, I thought I had posted a response in this thread. Anyway, mythical animal themes in alchemy are often referential, rather than essential, as in animism. The Fox or the Rabbit are tied to tales that make up the culture that tell them, in &quot;shamanistic&quot; societies. In alchemy, the same animal might encompass the folk tales, but the importance lies in the material and processes that are symbolized. The Fox is a solar creature, referring to gold and fire, and are thought to have the secret of the Elixir of Life. To an alchemist, that's not about chasing fox-spirits and meditating on the morals of the fable. To him, the Fox represents an alchemical mystery, or a process, or a ritual. To the Promethean, this could mean a Refinement Furnace of Aurum, or possibly Phosphorum or Mercurius, which reveals the secret of the Fox symbol. Fox sometimes slips the sick and elderly doses of the Elixir, so maybe he learns Medicine, or gains curative powers. There <i>could</i> be communions with Fox the spirit, but what it should have to teach the Promethean will have little to do with the Pilgrimage (Fox's lessons are rarely beneficial).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am liking this. Whether or not 1E Athanors are being converted into Refinement Furnaces, categorizing them according to Refinement rather than Lineage does make more sense.<br /> <br /> There's still the matter of the requirements for making them. And reagents, too..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T08:14:06-08:00","id":754055,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/741758-athanor-preview?p=742272#post742272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> but what about &quot;special groups&quot; for Prometheans?</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/741758-athanor-preview?p=742354#post742354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Promethean just doesn't seem like a game that would have or even need a z-splat.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/741758-athanor-preview?p=743265#post743265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Geist</b>, <b>Mummy</b>, <b>Demon</b>, and <b>Beast</b> all lack 'special rules groups.' </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> The purpose of the z-splats in games was to allow you to customize your character to a greater extent than normal. Clans and covenants were the large archetypes, while a bloodline was a variation on those giant archetypes. Same with Lodges, Legacies, old Athanors, kiths/Entitlements. In Geist, the krewe benefits has the same function as a z-axis. In Demon, well, its already a free-for-all, plus there's the Cypher, which functions the same as a z-axis. In Beast, you're pretty much required to customize your Hunger by default - it just doesn't get special rules - and the Families, Lair, and Legend are just as heavily customized. I don't know Mummy well enough to comment on it. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Beast is the only game I'm familiar with that doesn't allow some space for customization and growth in specific directions beyond the broad archetypes. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Refinements and Lineages are still general archetypes, not specific growths. The ability to move between Refinemetns, however, makes that any area that doesn't need to be refined, no pun intended. Promethean could benefit from smething along with Lineages - those are pretty stagnant.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Though, not sure if Athanors are going to occupy that space anymore. From the look of things, Athanors has basically become Promethean Magic Items. And I'm not sure if those items will fill that customziation need, or not. Not even the Refinement Furnaces. While I don't have anything against what amounts to alchemical magic item crafting, I'm not particularly attached to it either. These look like things that were generally acomplished by living NPCs in previous games as it was, and I find that I prefer the living to inanimate objects. YMMV<br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, though. I feel like every game except Vampire is getting the option to make magic items now. Werewolf, Mage, Promethean, Changeling, Hunter, Geist, Mummies, Demon... Beast don't seem to have any, but the jury is still out. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 11-04-2015, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T10:12:24-08:00","id":754388,"title":"","content":"Slot me in with the &quot;Old Athanors felt out of place anyways&quot; group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T17:52:52-08:00","id":755399,"title":"","content":"On customizing Prometheans:<br /> <br /> First, Refinements are getting Roles (?) that specialize their focus. <br /> <br /> Second: at the very least, I'm hoping that the Extempore will be highly customizable. More generally, remember that demiurges are going to be much more of a thing in 2e; hopefully, that means that even the other Lineages will be more flexible \u2014 or, barring that, will be presented as examples of what Lineages can be rather than being presented as a comprehensive list of all possible Lineages. The Dark Eras Lineage gives me hope in this regard. <br /> <br /> On Athanors as <b>Promethean</b>'s magic items: I like. My only concern is that they may not go far enough to suit me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T04:18:40-08:00","id":758393,"title":"","content":"Athanors helped specialize <u><i>Lineages</i></u>. Refinements, with their swapping nature, are actually less useful as a tool for specialization from this standpoint. I mean, its possible that there's other mechanics out there I haven't seen yet.<br /> <br /> Either way, however, its clear to me that Athanor simply aren't the same as they were in Promethean 1e, and the name is frankly misleading. Its an entirely new thing, that fills in a new role, not a reimagining of the old. Some of the things make sense - sanctuaries and lessons from gears are good for stories, and they did appear in 1e, so having them formalized is definitely a good thing. But I'm honestly not a fan of magic items in every game, and really couldn't care less about most of this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 11-06-2015, 07:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T15:15:15-08:00","id":759415,"title":"","content":"&quot;Customizability&quot; seems like a false argument. Lineage is just about the only static unrated trait in Promethean, and any Lineage can purchase the one explicit ability they provide, the Bestowment. Other than Pyros replenishment, little else is locked in to that stat, as far as choice goes. Refinement is fluid, there's no forced progression within Transmutation sets, and Prometheans aren't bound by human or inhuman social norms the way vampires and werewolves might be. Prometheans are highly individualistic; their personal journeys shape the narrative, and character choices are weighted differently for the Created than for the Awakened our the Lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}